  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-11-03T21:38:03.327Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Since build 1258, VRChat allowed desktop users to press the Y key to open up an on-screen chatbox keyboard to type.\n\nWhen typing text into an input field, pressing Y will open up the VRChat chatbox keyboard, stopping players from finishing up their message in the input field. This breaks text chat prefabs on certain worlds as well as other prefabs that make use of an input field that overrides the VRChat keyboard. Thus, this causes an inconvenience for desktop players.\n\nInput fields that override the on-screen keyboard should be allowed to also override VRC keybinds. In other words, VRChat should make sure that typing text in input fields do not trigger any of VRC's keybindings such as Y for the chatbox keyboard, R for the action menu, or V for opening the mic. Doing so will make text chat prefabs and other prefabs that make use of input fields more convenient.",
